wayland-backend's server on Radix, which has neither epoll nor kqueue:
a client is registered with nothing, and the server waits on each
client's own descriptor with poll(2) and dispatches it by its id, as
windowd does (ADR 0717). The descriptor the backend gives out for all of
its clients is one that is never ready, and dispatching all the clients
reads each of them.

